<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13465] Ignite cluster falls apart if two nodes segmented sequentially</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13465</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;After &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; sequential nodes failure leads to segmentation of other nodes in the cluster. Reproducer attached.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This ticked contains:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Reverted &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Fix for &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; to avoid the noted segmenttion.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Reverted &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; which depends on &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13134&quot; title=&quot;Fix connection recovery timeout.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13134&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13134&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13208&quot; title=&quot;Simplify IgniteSpiOperationTimeoutHelper&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13208&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13208&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
